# Effective field theory and experimental inference

Research date: 2026-10-23. This is an EFT and empirical-inference contribution to the draft category **Advanced QFT and supersymmetry** (`advanced-qft-and-supersymmetry`). It proposes a supplier-first route and records current source evidence. It does not add production carriers, publish a physics result, or certify any proof or experiment. The source frontier below includes reports I could inspect by 2026-10-23; that date does not imply a complete literature search or knowledge of later updates.

The boundary with the other research scopes is deliberate. The gauge-theory researcher owns non-Abelian bundles, gauge fixing, BRST/BV constructions, confinement, instantons, and the detailed anomaly derivations. The supersymmetry researcher owns the superalgebra, multiplets, superspace and transformations, vacuum structure, duality, breaking mechanisms, and supersymmetric phenomenology. The localization/BPS researcher owns those constructions and their physical interpretation. This note covers the EFT interfaces to those topics and the experimental reports needed to constrain EFT or supersymmetry models. An EFT application may depend on those subjects only at exact, reviewed interfaces.

## Existing material to reuse

The existing QFT pages fix important conventions and scopes. They should be consumed where their actual hypotheses are needed, without importing the entire QFT category as one prerequisite:

