| 2 | `aqft-eft-operators` / `aqft-eft-operators-examples` | Local operator spaces, symmetry invariants, IBP/EOM/field-redefinition quotient, and fixed-order power counting; follow foundations. |
| 3 | `aqft-eft-matching-running` / `aqft-eft-matching-running-examples` | Threshold matching, coefficient conventions, matrix RG evolution and scale independence; follow operator definitions and the exact finite scalar scale suppliers. |
| 4 | `aqft-smeft-heft` / `aqft-smeft-heft-examples` | SMEFT and HEFT model data, symmetry realizations, bases and expansions; follow operators and the gauge/SUSY owners' exact field/gauge interfaces. |
| 5 | `aqft-eft-amplitudes` / `aqft-eft-amplitudes-examples` | On-shell amplitude data, analyticity, positivity, and finite bootstrap constraints; follow model/power-counting definitions and use `qftx-on-shell-amplitudes` only at its conditional tree interface. |
| 6 | `aqft-eft-anomalies` / `aqft-eft-anomalies-examples` | Threshold/anomaly matching and Wess–Zumino EFT interface; follow the gauge and symmetry researchers' exact anomaly supplier pages and the stated `qftx` mathematical boundary. |
| 7 | `aqft-susy-effective-theories` / `aqft-susy-effective-theories-examples` | Supersymmetric Wilsonian actions, operator basis and threshold matching; follow the supersymmetry researcher's multiplet/action interfaces, not a formal BPS result alone. |
| 8 | `aqft-eft-experimental-inference` / `aqft-eft-experimental-inference-examples` | Operational experimental reports, EFT fits, SUSY search likelihoods and qualified empirical relations; use the statistical definitions and experiment items listed below. Keep theoretical model use explicit in each interpretation. |

Every examples page remains a leaf for logical dependencies under the physics page rules. If an experiment is reported before the theory it later tests, preserve that chronology through nonlogical `tested_by`/`supported_by` relations and place the theory-dependent prediction in a later item.

### A1 — EFT models, scales, and Wilsonian integration (`aqft-eft-foundations`)

Definitions should distinguish the microscopic model, its light fields, heavy fields/thresholds, regulator, Wilsonian scale `mu`, heavy mass/scale `M`, external energy `E`, and EFT cutoff `Lambda`; do not use those three scales interchangeably. Fix spacetime, signature, units, field spaces/representations, regularity, gauge/flavor symmetries, and normalization of the action. Define a Wilsonian action as a functional integral or rigorously specified finite-regulator pushforward over a declared high-mode sector. Define a local derivative expansion and its truncation as an asymptotic/organized approximation with named power-counting assumptions, not as a convergent series by default. Keep it distinct from a 1PI effective action and from a renormalized time-ordered product.

Candidate items: `def-aqft-model-and-scale-data`; `def-aqft-wilsonian-action`; `def-aqft-derivative-expansion-and-truncation`; `texp-aqft-finite-heavy-scalar-matching`; and `ex-aqft-gaussian-shell-matching` on the B page. The model item should explicitly state any functional measure or finite regulator and any physical adoptions. A thought-experiment result can derive a matching formula only conditionally on that construction; a mathematical proposition can handle the finite Gaussian integral without claiming it is nature's theory.

The first exact result should be the finite Gaussian match already proved in `lem-qftx-finite-heavy-gaussian-square` and `thm-qftx-heavy-derivative-bound`, with all spectral-band, positivity, normalization, and units hypotheses copied exactly. Add a separate proposition showing successive Gaussian shells compose via `prop-qftx-finite-gaussian-shell-semigroup`; do not infer a differentiable flow from that composition. `thm-qftx-truncated-rg-ode` may illustrate the solution of a given one-coupling truncation, only with its exact caveat that it neither supplies a coefficient nor bounds higher orders.

**Missing prerequisite:** a generic interacting Wilsonian mode split needs a declared regulated measure/action and well-defined integration over high modes; a continuum version needs existence and estimates for the measure/functionals used. A generic derivative-expansion remainder needs analyticity/locality assumptions and a normed observable class with an actual remainder proof. The current Gaussian theorem covers only a positive quadratic heavy sector and band-limited source. It supplies none of these general existence claims.

### A2 — Power counting, operator spaces, and redundancy (`aqft-eft-operators`)

Define a local operator as a specified scalar/gauge-invariant local polynomial in fields, covariant derivatives, and possibly spurions, with a stated engineering dimension and symmetry representation. State the coefficient ring (real/complex, formal/analytic), Grassmann grading, index contractions, and whether flavor tensors are independent. For a dimension-`d` operator in four dimensions, set the coefficient convention explicitly, e.g. `C_i(mu) O_i / Lambda^(d-4)`, or an equivalent convention with dimensionful Wilson coefficients. A change of convention must carry the corresponding units.

The operator basis is a quotient, not merely a list: specify the vector space of local monomials at fixed field content/order, the ideal/subspace of algebraic, Fierz, integration-by-parts/total-derivative, and leading-equations-of-motion relations being imposed, plus any global/gauge symmetry relations. Specify boundary conditions or compact-support assumptions under which total derivatives disappear from the action. A field redefinition must be a local invertible formal map with identity leading term, its order in `1/Lambda`, and the precise observable/S-matrix equivalence statement at the retained order. Do not use a classical EOM identity to assert equivalence of arbitrary off-shell Green functions or ignore a quantum Jacobian/anomaly premise.

Candidate items: `def-aqft-local-operator-and-dimension`; `def-aqft-operator-basis-quotient`; `prop-aqft-integration-by-parts-eom-and-field-redefinition-redundancy`; `thm-aqft-field-redefinition-observable-equivalence-at-fixed-order`; and `ex-aqft-operator-basis-reduction` on the B page. The last theorem must give a complete argument at the stated order and distinguish action-level equivalence from on-shell amplitude equivalence. The `def`/`prop` should work at fixed finite operator dimension before any infinite basis or Hilbert-series completion is asserted.

Root mathematical suppliers can provide polynomial rings, finite-dimensional representation decompositions, compact-group averaging, reductive invariant rings, formal series and quotient constructions. The missing EFT-specific argument is the identification of the physically appropriate operator quotient and the relation of each quotient operation to amplitudes or correlation functions. `Grzadkowski et al.` is the source for the dimension-six Warsaw classification under its stated Standard Model field content and baryon-number/flavor conventions; it is evidence for that literature result, not a locally proved basis theorem. Current published root/math scaffolds do not give the complete SMEFT basis classification, its flavor variants, or the general EOM/field-redefinition equivalence theorem as one ready EFT supplier.

Power counting must use the chosen counting scheme. Canonical dimension counting for a weakly coupled linear EFT, chiral/loop counting in HEFT, and a multi-scale SCET expansion are different systems. Each result must identify the order retained and which loops, insertions, and interferences contribute at that order. An `O(E^n/Lambda^n)` label needs a norm/observable domain and a bound or an explicitly formal asymptotic interpretation; power counting alone is not a numerical error estimate.

### A3 — Matching, threshold changes, and RG flow (`aqft-eft-matching-running`)

Define a renormalization scheme, scale-dependent coefficient vector, beta function/anomalous-dimension matrix, and matching map. Matching should equate a declared set of renormalized low-energy amplitudes/Green functions in the full and effective theories at a scale near a specified threshold, with identical IR regulators and renormalization conventions; it should state loop order, operator basis, mass expansion, and finite terms. Separate matching (changing field content/threshold) from running (evolving coefficients within one EFT). For several thresholds, state the ordered composition of matching and evolution maps.

Candidate items: `def-aqft-scheme-and-wilson-coefficients`; `def-aqft-threshold-matching-map`; `prop-aqft-matching-and-running-scale-independence`; `thm-aqft-truncated-coupled-rge-wellposedness`; `ex-aqft-qed-threshold-matching`; and a SUSY threshold example coordinated with the supersymmetry researcher. A one-loop SMEFT RGE coefficient is only a theorem after the basis, flavor assumptions, regulator/subtraction scheme, and computed matrix entries are explicit. The `Jenkins–Manohar–Trott` three-paper result gives one-loop dimension-six running for its assumptions; it is an external statement to reproduce or import only through the approved exact source protocol.

Small mathematical prerequisites: existence and uniqueness for finite-dimensional locally Lipschitz ODEs (already used by `thm-qftx-truncated-rg-ode`), matrix exponential/ordered evolution for the stated coefficient system, and formal power series for perturbative order bookkeeping. The larger missing mathematical/physical supplier is a local derivation of matching coefficients from a selected UV model and the corresponding full anomalous-dimension matrix. The existing formal scalar scale cocycle is not a substitute for this SMEFT calculation.

Required result obligation: prove that, through the stated perturbative/EFT truncation, a physical prediction is unchanged by changing the intermediate renormalization scale when the coefficient running, threshold matching, and matrix elements are combined consistently. Propagate omitted loop orders and higher-dimensional operators as separate theory uncertainties; do not label scheme-independent observables as exact Wilson coefficients.

### A4 — SMEFT, HEFT, and symmetry realization (`aqft-smeft-heft`)

For SMEFT, define the Standard Model gauge group and every representation, the linearly transforming Higgs doublet, the exact global/flavor/baryon/lepton assumptions, and a finite operator order. For HEFT/electroweak chiral EFT, define the nonlinear Goldstone coordinate/map for the chosen coset, the physical scalar singlet, its transformation law, and the chiral/loop power counting. State a concrete parameterization and coordinate patch for Goldstone fields when needed; do not identify it with an ordinary linear Higgs doublet by notation alone.

Candidate items: `post-aqft-smeft-model`; `def-aqft-warsaw-basis-contract`; `post-aqft-heft-model`; `def-aqft-chiral-power-counting`; `prop-aqft-smeft-as-restricted-heft-branch`; and `ex-aqft-smeft-heft-observable-map`. A restricted-branch proposition must list the coefficient/analyticity relations that realize the chosen linear-Higgs model inside the chosen HEFT parameterization. It must not assert that a finite SMEFT truncation parameterizes every HEFT or that every HEFT point has a weakly coupled UV completion.

`Grzadkowski et al. 2010` is the Warsaw-basis source, with the paper's assumptions about baryon number and flavor made explicit. `Buchalla, Cata, Krause 2015` supplies a systematic electroweak chiral/HEFT Lagrangian and loop power counting at NLO. The current library has neither classification as an exact local item. The local author must prove any selected reduction/correspondence or limit the page to definitions and source-faithful postulates with proof obligations left open.

### A5 — Amplitudes, dispersion relations, positivity, and bootstrap (`aqft-eft-amplitudes`)

Define the external stable states, LSZ/scattering data if such a construction is available, Mandelstam variables, crossing action, partial-wave normalization, amplitude analytic domain, poles/cuts, IR regulator and subtraction point. Start with a massive, gapped scalar elastic channel with a finite forward limit and an explicitly stated real-analytic, crossing-symmetric, unitary amplitude and polynomial high-energy bound. Derive one forward dispersion inequality in that narrow setting. Only after this base result may the scaffold add spinning/multifield channels, nonforward bounds, massless gauge particles or gravity.

Candidate items: `def-aqft-scattering-amplitude-input`; `lem-aqft-crossing-even-forward-amplitude`; `thm-aqft-gapped-scalar-forward-positivity`; `def-aqft-truncated-amplitude-bootstrap-problem`; `prop-aqft-finite-truncated-bootstrap-constraints`; and `ex-aqft-scalar-positivity-bound`. The B page should show both an allowed and a forbidden Wilson-coefficient region under exactly the same assumptions. `thm-qftx-rational-bcfw-residue` is reusable only for its conditional rational tree recursion. The new positivity proof still owes the contour argument, crossing/symmetrization, pole subtraction, subtractions at infinity, optical-theorem spectral sign, and low-energy coefficient identification.

The proof statement must carry its assumptions. Do not assert a universal sign for every Wilson coefficient: positivity constrains particular on-shell amplitude combinations. The usual mass-gap argument does not directly cover massless photon/graviton poles or massless cuts at `t=0`. For gravity, published proposals use extra IR/Regge assumptions and permit finite/controlled violations of strict positivity. Recent work also identifies polynomial boundedness/locality as a substantive premise; an exponentially bounded nonlocal amplitude can obey different bounds. The exact treatment of a given massless channel needs a local, source-backed proof or remains an open problem, never a silent citation leap.

### A6 — EFT gauge and anomaly interface (`aqft-eft-anomalies`)

This page is an interface, not a substitute for the gauge specialist's anomaly work. Define local gauge anomaly, anomaly polynomial/descent data, background/global symmetry anomaly, admissible counterterm, and Wess–Zumino functional in the exact chosen model. Distinguish an inconsistent gauge redundancy (which blocks the proposed quantum gauge theory absent a specified cancellation mechanism) from a global 't Hooft anomaly that an infrared effective theory must reproduce. When integrating out heavy chiral matter, state how its mass is generated and what degrees of freedom, Goldstone fields, or topological terms remain; ordinary power-suppressed decoupling is not automatic for anomaly data.

Candidate items: `def-aqft-anomaly-matching-data`; `prop-aqft-heavy-chiral-threshold-wess-zumino-match`; and `ex-aqft-heavy-fermion-anomaly-threshold`, but only after the gauge/anomaly researcher supplies the exact local definitions, anomaly normalization, and hypotheses. Reuse `qftx-bv-brst`, `qftx-anomaly-cocycles`, and `def-qftx-chiral-anomaly-interface` at their actual Abelian/scalar or purely mathematical interfaces. `D'Hoker–Farhi` and Wess–Zumino/Witten sources are candidate literature inputs; any coefficient-level statement must identify representations, symmetry breaking, regulator, descent convention, and admissible local counterterms. The current local QFT item does not prove the general non-Abelian threshold-matching statement.

### A7 — Supersymmetric EFT bridge (`aqft-susy-effective-theories`)

Use the supersymmetry researcher's exact `N=1`/other supersymmetry conventions and items. Define the allowed supersymmetric local operators in superspace, superpotential and Kähler/gauge-kinetic terms, the Wilsonian scale, and the selected UV/IR multiplets. A basis should be reduced by superspace integration by parts, superfield equations of motion, gauge identities, and allowed superfield redefinitions, with the same fixed-order amplitude/effective-action equivalence obligation as A2. Distinguish Wilsonian holomorphic data from 1PI quantities. If soft breaking is introduced, state the spurion representation and the exact power counting for soft terms; do not assume arbitrary soft breaking is a small perturbation without bounds.

Candidate items: `def-aqft-susy-wilsonian-action`; `prop-aqft-supersymmetric-threshold-matching`; `thm-aqft-wilsonian-superpotential-nonrenormalization` (only with the regulator, field content, gauge invariance, perturbative scope, and chiral/holomorphic definitions of the selected source); and `ex-aqft-soft-breaking-effective-operator`. Weinberg's perturbative theorem is a candidate source for the nonrenormalization obligation: it allows arbitrary gauge-invariant holomorphic `F(Phi,W)` in the Wilsonian Lagrangian, apart from one-loop gauge-coupling renormalization, subject to a cutoff preserving supersymmetry and gauge invariance. It is not a claim about nonperturbative corrections, arbitrary 1PI actions, or a model-independent absence of all running. Use the physical BPS bridge only after the localization/BPS researcher establishes it; the existing mathematical CoHA contract explicitly demands an additional dictionary and proves no physical index identity.

## Experimental accounts and inference obligations

Experiment pages must say what was recorded, how it was operationally defined, how the apparatus was calibrated, and which analysis/model yielded the reported constraint. A measurement and an EFT/SUSY prediction are different records. A likelihood fit is conditional on its event selection, background model, detector response, simulation, nuisance-parameter constraints/correlations, EFT truncation, and test statistic. A p-value is not the probability that the Standard Model or SUSY is true. A null search constrains only the specified channels and model parameterization.

