The proof statement must carry its assumptions. Do not assert a universal sign for every Wilson coefficient: positivity constrains particular on-shell amplitude combinations. The usual mass-gap argument does not directly cover massless photon/graviton poles or massless cuts at `t=0`. For gravity, published proposals use extra IR/Regge assumptions and permit finite/controlled violations of strict positivity. Recent work also identifies polynomial boundedness/locality as a substantive premise; an exponentially bounded nonlocal amplitude can obey different bounds. The exact treatment of a given massless channel needs a local, source-backed proof or remains an open problem, never a silent citation leap.

