+# Batch 24 authoring notes
+
+## Scope and plan comparison
+
+Assigned pair: aqft-eft-foundations / aqft-eft-foundations-examples, order 980, physics library. The current task, batch manifest, and plan-spec row agree on the title and all three page prerequisites: qftx-nonabelian-yang-mills-model, qft-c01, and qftx-heavy-field-eft. The design section and proposed-inventory page entry list only qftx-nonabelian-yang-mills-model. Followed the current plan and task manifest; the plan mismatch is recorded here and no shared plan was edited.
+
+The design calls for model and scale data, a Wilsonian action, a formal derivative expansion with no generic remainder claim, the bounded finite heavy-Gaussian match, and a separate finite Gaussian shell-composition proposition. The B item will work through exact finite-dimensional values. No continuum measure, universal matching theorem, empirical result, or differentiated flow is claimed.
+
+## Dependency-level evidence
+
+Read the stored batch dependency-level file. Its saved input hash is 872dc222b65e5b6f2b36bf2a5bff4231d1468980d1985ec86c50a80d02cb4914, but the scoped checker reports it stale. A read-only recomputation from current manifests gives hash d8a8801ef8ff295d5cd6725ab40865e0a957d033fb2743403a85f9e2e2d398bd and batch rows 13: level 0/no suppliers; 19: level 1/requires 2; 24: level 2/requires 19. The saved row for batch 19 instead says requires 13. This is shared scheduling evidence owned by the run owner; it was left untouched. The assigned pair's current page-level priority is 2.
+
+Planned item-level levels, from actual local item dependencies: def-aqft-model-and-scale-data 1 (uses the current batch-2 gauge-data definition); def-aqft-wilsonian-action 2; def-aqft-derivative-expansion-and-truncation 3; prop-aqft-finite-gaussian-shell-composition 0 (only outside-run math suppliers); texp-aqft-finite-heavy-scalar-matching 4; ex-aqft-gaussian-shell-matching 5. These will be mechanically checked against the completed batch manifest.
+
+## Supplier review and open page edge
+
+qft-c01 is published; only the exact def-qft-framework-units unit and normalization statement is used. Its unrelated Born-instrument and autonomous-evolution portions are not EFT premises.
+
+qftx-heavy-field-eft is published. Read the complete actual statements and proofs of lem-qftx-finite-heavy-gaussian-square, def-qftx-heavy-gaussian-data, thm-qftx-heavy-derivative-bound, def-qftx-finite-gaussian-shell-transform, and prop-qftx-finite-gaussian-shell-semigroup. Their finite-dimensional, positive-kernel, spectral-band, normalization, AC/CC, and units hypotheses are carried explicitly. The positive spectral-calculus and PVM-homomorphism inputs used by the derivative bound and heavy-data proof were also inspected. The mixed-effects-and-longitudinal-models page is present in the immutable math-import record; the exact item-level bridge is its multivariate-normal definition and nondegenerate Gaussian-density theorem, both used by the finite Gaussian square lemma. No other mixed-model result is used. qftx-analytic-prerequisites supplies the positive spectral calculus used in the heavy-data proof; qft-ir02 is only a declared page-level prerequisite and supplies no item used in these arguments.
+
+The qftx-nonabelian-yang-mills-model A page is a current batch-19 prerequisite, but its item inventory is empty. The planned postulate post-qftx-nonabelian-yang-mills-model and its two planned classical consumers have no current carriers on that page; loadStep1Record shows the empty page and step1Decision reports the planned postulate readiness record missing. The exact planned postulate selects G, P, M, metric, invariant bilinear form, matter representations, units, coupling, action, boundary conditions, and physical scope, and explicitly does not imply a quantum continuum model. Its own current prerequisite page qftx-gauge-geometry is in batch 2; its five A-page mathematical items have current ready records. Draft status alone is not a gap. The B24 A-page requirement on the missing batch-19 page remains an open page dependency. The finite scalar calculations do not use a Yang–Mills equation or action, so no absent physical result is asserted or substituted.
+
+## Sources
+
+- David B. Kaplan, Five lectures on effective field theory, https://arxiv.org/pdf/nucl-th/0510023; full 79-page lecture-notes PDF retrieved. Read §§1.1–1.2 and §2.2, including the low-energy local-operator definition and the finite matching discussion. Supports the three definitions and the conditional physical interpretation.
+- C. P. Burgess, Introduction to Effective Field Theory, https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/0701053; full 55-page review PDF retrieved. Read §§2.2.1–2.2.5 and the relevant power-counting passage in §3. Supports the finite Wilson-action definition, distinction between matching and scale evolution, and the model-specific derivative expansion. It does not prove the local finite Gaussian claims.
+- Nima Moshayedi, Quantum Field Theory and Functional Integrals, https://arxiv.org/pdf/1902.08652; full 88-page PDF retrieved. Read §11.2, printed pp. 44–47, including Proposition 11.2.2(1) and its finite Gaussian exponential-moment proof. The source's separate dense-exponential argument in Proposition 11.2.2(2) is not used; shell composition follows the complete current local product-measure/characteristic-function/Tonelli proof.
+- An optional Skinner chapter PDF fetch was refused by the browser reader because its 18,511,004-byte response exceeded that reader's content limit. Searched for an alternative and retrieved Moshayedi's complete arXiv PDF; no authored claim depends on Skinner, and the exact local Gaussian proofs were inspected. No retry of the optional Skinner URL was made after the complete alternative was available.
+
